fety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":12,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"PKT-0056 is done: the `word/js-api/js-api-forms.html` suite now runs in the oracle and passes 27/27. It didn't need the factory change the packet expected.\n\n**What changed**\n- **Oracle script** (`.theseus/oracle/sdkjs-word.sh`): it now does a shallow clone of `github.com/Euro-Office/sdkjs-forms` into `external/sdkjs-forms` if that folder is missing. It then builds `develop` with `SDK_ADDONS=../../sdkjs-forms`, the same command upstream CI uses. Like `external/sdkjs`, the clone is not committed.\n- **Rebuild trigger:** after a build with the addon, the script writes a marker file, `develop/.theseus-addons-forms`. Worktrees whose `develop` was built without the addon don't have it, so they rebuild once on their next run.\n- **Skip removed:** the local skip of `js-api-forms.html` is gone from `sdkjs-word-run.cjs`.\n- **Docs:** `adapter/environment.md` now explains how the forms addon gets there.\n\n**Result:** I ran the acceptance command `.theseus/oracle/sdkjs-word.sh` and all 42 of 42 suites passed (6195/6195 assertions, 129s). The 41 suites that passed before still pass, so the contract holds.\n\n**Wrap-up:** the Executor log and the lesson for the Atlas are written in the packet. My friction line is in, after one fix to its field format, and `theseus validate` reports no errors. There are two commits on the branch.\n\n**Two things to know:**\n- The forms clone is not pinned to a version; it takes the current head (5c2f5a0), while `sdkjs` is at d9e810c. If the two drift apart, the forms suite could start failing. Pinning it would take a factory mirror.\n- A fresh worktree needs network access the first time the oracle runs, to make the clone.\n\n**Lesson for the Atlas:** the sdkjs-word oracle depends on the sdkjs-forms addon and clones it on first run.","ttft_ms":2055,"type":"result","duration_ms":188987,"uuid":"331df73a-0b02-4c27-a279-1b0e9de20cb7","ttft_stream_ms